  "source": {
    "plan": "Callboard row 2026-11-19 (storyhowto, story-howto, paper): bring your sides scans the file first, tick only your scenes; the script's map moves a scene to another act",
    "app": "Ghost Light web preview (ghostlight-web/serve.sh) at main 50a1c23, dark theme, demo account, 2026-11-14; app/sides.tsx and app/edit-map.tsx read first",
    "flows": "flows/sides-you-are-in-two-scenes.json (scan, tick, build) then flows/sides-move-the-letter-scene.json (the map); shots -> public/story/2026-11-19-you-are-in-two-scenes/*.png. mapbuild.png (the map scrolled to its Build button) was captured by a second scan of the same file with the same three taps, nothing built",
    "script": "flows/sides/The_Rivals.txt: Sheridan, The Rivals (1775), Acts I to V as stored in plays.id 234 (Gutenberg 24761), public domain; preface, prologue and epilogue left out",
    "checked": "the board said four scenes; the scan found 14 scenes and Lucy speaks in two (Act 1 Scene 2, 18 speeches; Act 2 Scene 2, 19 speeches, where she hands Sir Lucius the letter), so the hook says two. 112 pages is the drawn script in the story, not a number from the app",
    "app_result": "the map listed 14 scenes under ACT 1 to ACT 5; Act 1 Scene 2 and Act 2 Scene 2 ticked, 'Build 2 scenes', read in about 80 seconds into THE RIVALS, 2 scenes ('Lydia's Literary Pursuits', 'Rivalry and Romantic Schemes'). In the map the pencil on the second scene, Move to another act, Act 1, Save: both scenes now sit under ACT 1 on the demo shelf ('reset the map to how it was read' puts it back)",
    "not_shown": "dragging by the handle (the pencil's Move to another act is shown instead); the per scene pencil in the Scene room (the map is opened from the script row's pencil); the run itself",
    "preview": "web-preview.patch regenerated against Ghost Light main as one commit: the multipart shim now lives in sendFile and sendable (scan, upload-background, scene-map, add-scenes all use them)",
    "voice": "George, one take at stability 0.5, listened back with Scribe (0.97); sped up 1.2x with fit_take.py; take00.orig.mp3 kept locally, not committed",
    "new_scene_types": "thud (read-through table, the script lands; calm = your slim pages), dry (highlighter runs dry), scatter (pages in the air)",
    "end": "specs/2026-11-19-you-are-in-two-scenes-end.json, joined with scripts/join.sh; the end line is cut from the take"
  }
